WEBVTT

00:00:00.180 --> 00:00:02.438 line:92% position:50% size:90%
Turn one paper result into

00:00:02.438 --> 00:00:04.245 line:92% position:50% size:90%
a useful learning reflection.

00:00:05.180 --> 00:00:07.676 line:92% position:50% size:90%
After a practice close, open

00:00:07.676 --> 00:00:09.672 line:92% position:50% size:90%
Journal beneath the chart.

00:00:11.180 --> 00:00:12.374 line:92% position:50% size:90%
Start with the newest

00:00:12.374 --> 00:00:13.569 line:92% position:50% size:90%
close at the top.

00:00:17.180 --> 00:00:20.155 line:92% position:50% size:90%
Read the trade direction and instrument together.

00:00:23.180 --> 00:00:25.295 line:92% position:50% size:90%
Check the volume that was closed.

00:00:29.180 --> 00:00:31.459 line:92% position:50% size:90%
Then read the paper result.

00:00:31.459 --> 00:00:33.282 line:92% position:50% size:90%
Profit alone proves little.

00:00:35.180 --> 00:00:37.148 line:92% position:50% size:90%
A partial close can create

00:00:37.148 --> 00:00:39.117 line:92% position:50% size:90%
another row for one position.

00:00:41.180 --> 00:00:43.492 line:92% position:50% size:90%
For a learning record, use

00:00:43.492 --> 00:00:45.804 line:92% position:50% size:90%
your Academy lesson's practice notes.

00:00:47.180 --> 00:00:48.756 line:92% position:50% size:90%
Write one thing you

00:00:48.756 --> 00:00:50.331 line:92% position:50% size:90%
would review next time.

00:00:53.180 --> 00:00:55.162 line:92% position:50% size:90%
Save your reflection, and ask

00:00:55.162 --> 00:00:57.145 line:92% position:50% size:90%
a lesson question if needed.
